<title>SINGAPORE: Photronics opens $15 mln Singapore plant.</title>
<headline>Photronics opens $15 mln Singapore plant.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. photomask maker Photronics Inc said on Wednesday it had opened a US$15 million plant in Singapore, its first in Southeast Asia.</p>
<p>Photomasks are high-precision quartz plates that contain microscopic images of electronic circuits and are a key element in the manufacture of semiconductors.</p>
<p>Photronics said more investment in the plant was planned, but gave no further details.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
